<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantius I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 250–<a href="/years/306">306</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Constantius Chlorus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantius I, known as Chlorus, was a Roman emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetrarchy">Tetrarchy</a>, made Caesar in the west under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximian">Maximian</a> in 293 and senior emperor in 305. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a> from the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carausius">Carausius</a> in 293 and recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allectus">Allectus</a> in 296. He died at York in 306, where his troops proclaimed his son Constantine emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantius-i.jpg" alt="Constantius I" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marie-Lan Nguyen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Constantius_Chlorus_Ny_Carlsberg_Glyptotek_IN836.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Constantius Chlorus</b> campaigned against the Picts in 305–306, in 367 they took part in the barbarian conspiracy that overran the province, and Magnus Maximus fought them around 382.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-picts">Kingdom of the Picts · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Constantine the Great was proclaimed emperor at York in 306, after his father <b>Constantius</b> died there while campaigning in Britain.</blockquote><a href="/empire/roman-britain">Roman Britain · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>In 293 <b>Constantius Chlorus</b> captured Boulogne, and Carausius was murdered by his finance minister Allectus, who took power.</blockquote><a href="/state/carausian-empire">Carausian Empire</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Dardania, in what is now <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eboracum">Eboracum</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.32,21.88&amp;year=286" aria-label="Dardania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5077 627 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Constantius I"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5527 897h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5527 897h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.32,21.88&amp;year=286">What was here in 286 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
